Error [jet.HoleHeaderEffect]: This `if` table header calls `noisy`, which has an effect
  --> Tests/UI/E0442_dispatch_hole_header_effect.jet:9:8
    |
  9 |     if noisy(n) % <> == 0 {
    |        ^^^^^
 Why: A hole table runs its header once for each arm it tries, so `noisy` would run again for every arm
 Fix: Name the value first: `value: noisy(n)` on the line above, then read `value` in the header
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0442
